---
/**
 * A published system.
 *
 * ONE STATIC PAGE SERVING EVERY POST. `/p/k7f3q9` is rewritten onto this route
 * by netlify.toml — a 200, not a redirect, so the address the coach published
 * stays in the bar. Exactly the shape `/c/*` and `/s/*` already use, and the
 * same dev/production difference: the rewrite is applied by `netlify dev` on
 * :8888 and NOT by `astro dev` on :4321, which is why `postIdFromPath` also
 * accepts `?p=<id>`.
 *
 * `noindex` FOR NOW, and it comes off in the same commit as the OG card. There
 * is no page here for a crawler to read — only a shell that fills itself in on
 * the client — so every post would look to one like a duplicate of every other.
 * §5a of docs/SOCIAL.md is where that is fixed, by a Netlify function that
 * serves this route's head with the post's own title, summary and board image.
 *
 * NOT `bare`. The shared viewer hides the site nav because a coach presenting
 * off it does not want it on the wall behind them. This is the opposite: a page
 * read by a stranger who may never have heard of us, and the nav is how they
 * find out what this place is.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PostView from '../../studio/viewer/PostView'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="A system"
  description="A football system published on Total Football."
  path="/p/"
  noindex
>
  <div class="min-h-[70vh] bg-paper-deep">
    <PostView client:only="react" />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
